<translate>

Use this guide for the Enshrouded Dedicated Server installed on Windows through Steam or managed by a Windows hosting panel. First complete [[Multiplayer: Install server files|the shared server-file setup]].

== Open the server's mod settings ==

On the Windows PC, open PowerShell in the folder containing the ShroudForge release files. Run the command below and replace the example path with the folder containing the server's <code>enshrouded_server.exe</code>:

<pre>
.\shroudforge\shroudforge.exe --root "D:\Games\EnshroudedServer\server" --desktop --target server
</pre>

The command opens ShroudForge settings for that server installation. Enable the mod there. The <code>--target server</code> option selects the Dedicated Server installation even if your PC also has the game client.

== Start the server ==

Start the Dedicated Server using its normal Steam or hosting-panel method. The server loads ShroudForge and its mods from its own installation folder.

The Proton-only <code>WINEDLLOVERRIDES</code> setting is not needed for the Windows Dedicated Server.

== Check the server log ==

Read <code>shroudforge/logs/shroudforge-server.log</code> in the server folder. Check the log after startup if ShroudForge or a mod does not appear to load.

== Use mods on the client ==

The Dedicated Server and each player's PC are separate installations. Install a mod on the PC as well when its instructions or process targets require the client to run it.

